We are legally obliged to keep some information for the time being. Under
Article 17(3)(e) of the GDPR, the right to erasure does not apply where we need
the data to establish, exercise or defend legal claims.

This is a delay, not a refusal. Your request stands. As soon as the obligation
ends, the deletion runs automatically and we will confirm it to you — you do not
need to ask again.

While you wait:

  - Your account is unaffected. Nothing has changed about how you use it.
  - We are not doing anything new with your data. The obligation is to KEEP it,
    not to use it.
  - Your other rights are unaffected. You can still ask for a copy of your data
    or object to how it is processed.

If you want to know more about the delay, reply to this message and a person
will answer.
